From ab1dba2efca55b6c03c9c3ce610b6a8b080fdb36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:28:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): sidebar sort key ranks each lane row by its own
 fields

Lanes, gateway groups and project overview previews ranked by
$sidebarSessionRankIds, an id order built from the loaded $sessions page
only. Rows outside that page (backend previews, other gateways' rows) were
folded in by their position in the recency-sorted pool, so under the
'created' sort they moved every time activity reordered the lane.

$sidebarSessionRank exposes the key as a function of the row; rankSessions
sorts by it (ties keep arrival order). The flat list keeps the id order.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
